<section class="saas-legal-page">
  <div class="saas-container saas-page-shell">
    <div class="saas-page-hero">
      <p class="saas-legal-kicker">Photo to Sticker</p>

      <h1>Photo to Sticker AI Generator</h1>

      <p>
        Turn a clear photo or portrait into a sticker-style image. Use the photo to sticker workflow
        for avatars, creator badges, pet stickers, profile icons, and expressive chat artwork.
      </p>
      <a class="saas-button saas-button-primary" href="/#upload">Upload a Photo</a>
    </div>

    <div class="saas-info-grid">
      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Photo-ready subjects</h2>

        <p>
          Portraits, pets, objects, and simple character photos work best when one subject is easy
          to recognize and the background is not busy.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>Prompt guided style</h2>

        <p>
          Add a short prompt to guide the sticker look, such as clean outline, cute avatar, bright
          reaction sticker, or simple background.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="saas-info-panel">
        <h2>History and downloads</h2>

        <p>
          Finished photo stickers are saved in history so you can retry, favorite, regenerate, and
          download PNG or WebP files.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>How to turn a photo into a sticker</h2>

      <ol>
        <li>Sign in so your free or paid credits can be checked before generation.</li>
        <li>Upload a JPG or PNG photo with one main subject, good light, and minimal blur.</li>
        <li>Add an optional prompt that describes the final sticker use case or style.</li>
        <li>Generate the photo sticker, then download PNG or WebP from your history.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Photo sticker prompt examples</h2>

      <div class="saas-prompt-list">
        <code>photo to sticker, friendly portrait, clean white border, simple background</code>
        <code>pet photo sticker, playful expression, rounded icon style, crisp outline</code>
        <code>creator badge from photo, expressive face, bright sticker colors</code>
        <code>object photo sticker, cute mascot style, clean silhouette, soft shadow</code>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="saas-seo-block">
      <h2>Best photo tips</h2>

      <p>
        The strongest photo stickers start with a readable subject. Avoid crowded group photos,
        extreme darkness, heavy blur, or tiny subjects. A portrait or subject-focused image gives
        the generator a clearer shape to stylize.
      </p>

      <p>
        If the result needs to work as an avatar or chat sticker, keep the prompt focused on the
        expression, outline, and final use case instead of adding too many scene details.
      </p>

      <div class="saas-related-links">
        <.link navigate={~p"/face-to-sticker"}>Face to Sticker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/ai-avatar-sticker"}>AI Avatar Sticker</.link>
        <.link navigate={~p"/transparent-sticker-maker"}>PNG and WebP Downloads</.link>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="saas-faq">
      <details open>
        <summary>What kind of photo works best?</summary>

        <p>
          A bright photo with one main subject works best. Portraits, pets, products, and simple
          objects are easier to convert into sticker-style artwork than crowded scenes.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Can I turn any photo into a sticker?</summary>

        <p>
          The generator is strongest for portraits and subject-focused photos. Very busy, blurry,
          or low-light images may be harder to turn into a clean sticker.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details>
        <summary>Where do finished photo stickers go?</summary>

        <p>
          Completed photo stickers appear in your sticker history with download, favorite,
          regenerate, and retry options.
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
